# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
# Keysas firewall — udev rules for USB storage control
#
# Strategy (two layers):
#
#   Layer 1 (this rule): set UDISKS_IGNORE=1 on every USB block partition as
#   soon as the kernel announces it.  This prevents udisks2 / the desktop
#   environment from auto-mounting the device before the daemon has had time
#   to check its certificate.  It also prevents the device from appearing in
#   file managers.
#
#   Layer 2 (daemon): the keysas-firewall daemon receives the same udev event
#   via its netlink socket, reads the Keysas signature from sector 1 of the
#   raw block device (no mount required), and verifies it against the USB CA.
#
#     - Certified key   → daemon mounts the partition read-only under
#                         /run/keysas/media/<devname>/ and notifies the GUI.
#     - Uncertified key → daemon writes 0 to
#                         /sys/…/<usb_parent>/authorized, which causes the
#                         kernel to disconnect the USB device entirely.
#
# This combination closes the race window between device appearance and
# policy enforcement without requiring any eBPF or kernel module.
#
# Note: SUBSYSTEMS=="usb" (plural) walks the sysfs parent chain — more
# reliable than ENV{ID_BUS}=="usb" which is not always propagated to
# partition events (sdb1) by all udev versions.

SUBSYSTEM=="block", ACTION=="add", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ENV{UDISKS_IGNORE}="1"
